-- Task set-witness-nested-let-classifier: the comparison that constrains x
-- sits under an intermediate named binding (`draw y = x + 1.0`), so the
-- set-valued witness engine has to invert THROUGH the inner let rather than
-- match a comparison directly under the outer one. Must agree with its
-- flattened single-let twin `if (x + 1.0) > 0.0 ...`: Phi(1).
main = draw x = Normal in draw y = x + 1.0 in if y > 0.0 then 1.0 else 0.0
